    <article class="doc">
        <h2 id="partition">Step 1: Partition, format, and mount</h2>

        <p>
            Create two partitions with <code>cfdisk</code>: an EFI System
            Partition as the first partition and an <code>ext4</code> root
            partition as the second. The EFI partition is mounted at
            <code>/boot</code>.
        </p>

        <pre><code>cfdisk --zero /dev/nvme0n1
mkfs.vfat -F32 /dev/nvme0n1p1
mkfs.ext4 -F -l "Vylen Linux" /dev/nvme0n1p2

mount /dev/nvme0n1p2 /mnt
mount /dev/nvme0n1p1 /mnt/boot --mkdir</code></pre>

        <h2 id="rootfs">Step 2: Install the root filesystem</h2>

        <p>
            Place the Vylen root filesystem archive in the live environment,
            then extract it into <code>/mnt</code> and enter the installed
            system:
        </p>

        <pre><code>{% if rootfs %}curl -L -C - -O '{{ rootfs.tarball }}'
curl -L -C - -O '{{ rootfs.b3sum }}'

# Verify hash sums
b3sum -c {{ rootfs.b3sum_filename }}

{% endif %}tar xvJpf {{ rootfs.tarball_filename }} -C /mnt
/mnt/usr/bin/xchroot /mnt /usr/bin/bash</code></pre>

        <h2 id="base">Step 3: Configure the base system</h2>

        <p>
            Set the hardware clock, timezone, keyboard, repository metadata,
            package database, filesystem table, locale, and initial passwords.
        </p>

        <pre><code>hwclock --hctosys --utc
ln -snf /usr/share/zoneinfo/Region/City /etc/localtime
loadkeys -q us

sed -i -E '/\/extra[[:space:]]/s/^#//' /etc/emerald.repo

emerald sync
emerald upgrade emerald -y
emerald sysup -y

blkid /dev/nvme0n1p*
vi /etc/fstab</code></pre>

        <p>
            Use the UUID values from <code>blkid</code> in
            <code>/etc/fstab</code>:
        </p>

        <pre><code>UUID=&lt;efi-uuid&gt;  /boot  vfat  defaults  0 0
UUID=&lt;root-uuid&gt; /      ext4  defaults  0 1</code></pre>

        <p>
            Replace <code>Region/City</code> with the required zoneinfo path.
            Enable a locale, generate it, set the root password, and create the
            first user:
        </p>

        <pre><code>sed -i 's/^#en_US\.UTF-8 UTF-8/en_US.UTF-8 UTF-8/' /etc/locales
genlocales

passwd
useradd -m -G users,wheel,audio,video,usb,render -s /usr/bin/bash user
passwd user</code></pre>

        <p>Replace <code>user</code> with the name of the account to create.</p>
        <h2 id="boot">Step 4: Install the kernel and create the EFI entry</h2>

        <p>
            The root filesystem tools are already available from the core
            installation. The kernel and EFI boot-entry utility are provided by
            the extra repository, which was enabled in the previous step:
        </p>

        <pre><code>emerald install linux efibootmgr</code></pre>

        <p>
            Create the UEFI boot entry. Replace
            <code>&lt;root-uuid&gt;</code> with the root filesystem UUID from
            <code>blkid</code>:
        </p>

        <pre><code>efibootmgr \
    --create \
    --disk /dev/nvme0n1 \
    --part 1 \
    --label "Vylen Linux (linux)" \
    --loader '/vmlinuz-linux' \
    --unicode 'initrd=\\initrd-linux.img root=UUID=&lt;root-uuid&gt; rw rootfstype=ext4'</code></pre>

        <h2 id="finish">Step 5: Finish installation</h2>
        <p>Leave the installed system, unmount the target, and reboot from the new Vylen installation:</p>

        <pre><code>exit
umount /mnt -l
reboot</code></pre>
    </article>
</section>
